# Stage 3 Walkthrough — Real Postgres via MCP

## What Was Built

### Schema (`init_db.py`)
Six tables, all created fresh and seeded on every `python init_db.py` run:

| Table | Key Columns |
|---|---|
| `properties` | property_id, address |
| `units` | unit_id, **property_id (FK)**, unit_number |
| `tenants` | tenant_id, phone_or_email, name, **unit_id (FK)** |
| `maintenance_tickets` | ticket_id, tenant_id, property_id, unit_id, category, description, urgency, permission_to_enter, pets_present, **status='OPEN'**, source_channel, created_by, **idempotency_key (UNIQUE)** |
| `ticket_status_log` | ticket_id, old_status, new_status, timestamp |
| `audit_logs` | log_id, action, details, actor, before_state (JSONB), after_state (JSONB), timestamp |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Join logic (confirmed):** `tenants.unit_id → units.unit_id → units.property_id → properties.property_id`.  
> Tenants link to `unit_id` only. `property_id` on a ticket is resolved inside `create_ticket` by querying `units`, never fabricated.

---

### MCP Server (`mcp_server.py`)
- Uses `psycopg.AsyncConnection` (per-call, no pool) to avoid Windows `ProactorEventLoop` incompatibility.
- Forces `WindowsSelectorEventLoopPolicy` at module import time before `FastMCP` runs.
- **Tools exposed:**
  - `lookup_tenant(phone_or_email)` — tenant → unit join, returns real DB IDs
  - `lookup_property(unit_id)` — unit → property join
  - `create_ticket(...)` — idempotency + duplicate check + insert + audit log, all in one transaction
- `write_audit_log` is **internal only** — the graph never calls it directly.

### LangGraph Nodes (`nodes.py`)
- `receptionist_node` stores both display name (`tenant_identity`) and real DB foreign keys (`db_tenant_id`, `db_unit_id`) in state.
- `request_builder_node` passes `db_tenant_id`/`db_unit_id` to the ticket payload, falling back to conversation-extracted values for unknown callers.
- `ticket_creation_node` generates a `uuid4` idempotency key client-side and calls `create_ticket` over the MCP protocol — never imports or calls the server function directly.

